.TH FL-SCREENSHOT 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-screenshot \- take a screenshot
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-screenshot\fR [\fB\-\-area\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBDeprecated.\fR Use \fBfl-snip \-\-full\fR or \fBfl-snip \-\-area\fR instead;
this wrapper will be removed in a later release.
.PP
Kept for old key bindings and scripts: runs \fBfl-snip \-\-full\fR (or \fBfl-snip \-\-area\fR),
which saves the screenshot to ~/Pictures/Screenshots, copies it to the clipboard and prints
the file's path.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-snip\fR(1), \fBfl-wm\fR(1)
